        `how the entry gives the meaning`                 IS `the entry says it means`
        `the case or context in which the entry applies`  IS NOTHING
        `the things the entry names`                      IS LIST "a day which is not a Sunday"
        `what the entry points at`                        IS EMPTY
-- Worked out in ie-interpretation-time.l4 (`is a week-day`).

-- src:247 | “writing” includes printing, typewriting, lithography, photography, and other modes of representing or reproducing words in visible form and any information kept in a non-legible form, whether stored electronically or otherwise, which is capable by any means of being reproduced in a legible form;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "writing" (src:247)
`Part 1 entry: writing` MEANS
    `An entry in the Schedule` WITH
        `the word defined`                                IS "writing"
        `the part of the Schedule`                        IS 1
        `how the entry gives the meaning`                 IS `the entry says it includes`
        `the case or context in which the entry applies`  IS NOTHING
        `the things the entry names`                      IS LIST "printing", "typewriting", "lithography", "photography", "other modes of representing or reproducing words in visible form", "other modes of representing words in visible form", "other modes of reproducing words in visible form", "any information kept in a non-legible form, whether stored electronically or otherwise, which is capable by any means of being reproduced in a legible form"
        `what the entry points at`                        IS EMPTY

-- F48: "other modes of representing or reproducing words in visible form" and the two modes it joins are all members. "any information kept in a non-legible form, whether stored
-- electronically or otherwise, which is capable by any means of being reproduced in a legible form" is one: "whether stored electronically or otherwise" qualifies it and lists nothing.

-- src:248 | “year”, when used without qualification, means a period of 12 months beginning on the 1st day of January in any year.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "year" (src:248)
`Part 1 entry: year` MEANS
    `An entry in the Schedule` WITH
        `the word defined`                                IS "year"
        `the part of the Schedule`                        IS 1
        `how the entry gives the meaning`                 IS `the entry says it means`
        `the case or context in which the entry applies`  IS JUST "when used without qualification"
        `the things the entry names`                      IS LIST "a period of 12 months beginning on the 1st day of January in any year"
        `what the entry points at`                        IS EMPTY
-- Worked out in ie-interpretation-time.l4 (`the year containing`, and the years limb of `the last day of a period of`).

-- src:185 | Interpretation of words and expressions in Schedule. 21.—(1) In an enactment, a word or expression to which a particular meaning, construction or effect is assigned in Part 1 of the Schedule has the meaning, construction or effect so assigned to it.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 21(1) (src:185)
GIVEN w IS A `A word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule`
GIVETH AN `An entry in the Schedule`
`the Part 1 entry for` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `affidavit`                             THEN `Part 1 entry: affidavit`
    WHEN `British statute`                       THEN `Part 1 entry: British statute`
    WHEN `Circuit Court`                         THEN `Part 1 entry: Circuit Court`
    WHEN `commencement`                          THEN `Part 1 entry: commencement`
    WHEN `Constitution`                          THEN `Part 1 entry: Constitution`
    WHEN `Dail Eireann`                          THEN `Part 1 entry: Dail Eireann`
    WHEN `District Court`                        THEN `Part 1 entry: District Court`
    WHEN `financial year`                        THEN `Part 1 entry: financial year`
    WHEN `Government`                            THEN `Part 1 entry: Government`
    WHEN `Great Britain`                         THEN `Part 1 entry: Great Britain`
    WHEN `High Court`                            THEN `Part 1 entry: High Court`
    WHEN `land`                                  THEN `Part 1 entry: land`
    WHEN `local financial year`                  THEN `Part 1 entry: local financial year`
    WHEN `midnight`                              THEN `Part 1 entry: midnight`
    WHEN `Minister of the Government`            THEN `Part 1 entry: Minister of the Government`
    WHEN `month`                                 THEN `Part 1 entry: month`
    WHEN `oath`                                  THEN `Part 1 entry: oath`
    WHEN `Oireachtas`                            THEN `Part 1 entry: Oireachtas`
    WHEN `ordnance map`                          THEN `Part 1 entry: ordnance map`
    WHEN `President`                             THEN `Part 1 entry: President`
    WHEN `pre-union Irish statute`               THEN `Part 1 entry: pre-union Irish statute`
    WHEN `rateable valuation`                    THEN `Part 1 entry: rateable valuation`
    WHEN `rules of court`                        THEN `Part 1 entry: rules of court`
    WHEN `Saorstat Eireann statute`              THEN `Part 1 entry: Saorstat Eireann statute`
    WHEN `Seanad Eireann`                        THEN `Part 1 entry: Seanad Eireann`
    WHEN `statutory declaration`                 THEN `Part 1 entry: statutory declaration`
    WHEN `Supreme Court`                         THEN `Part 1 entry: Supreme Court`
    WHEN `swear`                                 THEN `Part 1 entry: swear`
    WHEN `week`                                  THEN `Part 1 entry: week`
    WHEN `week-day`                              THEN `Part 1 entry: week-day`
    WHEN `writing`                               THEN `Part 1 entry: writing`
    WHEN `year`                                  THEN `Part 1 entry: year`

§ `Schedule Part 2: the defined words`

-- src:250 | “Companies Acts” means the Companies Acts 1963 to 2001 and every other enactment which is to be read together with any of those Acts;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "Companies Acts" (src:250)
`Part 2 entry: Companies Acts` MEANS
    `An entry in the Schedule` WITH
        `the word defined`                                IS "Companies Acts"
        `the part of the Schedule`                        IS 2
        `how the entry gives the meaning`                 IS `the entry says it means`
        `the case or context in which the entry applies`  IS NOTHING
        `the things the entry names`                      IS LIST "the Companies Acts 1963 to 2001", "every other enactment which is to be read together with any of those Acts"
        `what the entry points at`                        IS LIST "the Companies Acts 1963 to 2001"

-- src:251 | “full age”, in relation to a person, means the time when the person attains the age of 18 years or sooner marries, or any time after either event;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "full age" (src:251)
`Part 2 entry: full age` MEANS
    `An entry in the Schedule` WITH
        `the word defined`                                IS "full age"
        `the part of the Schedule`                        IS 2
        `how the entry gives the meaning`                 IS `the entry says it means`
        `the case or context in which the entry applies`  IS JUST "in relation to a person"
        `the things the entry names`                      IS LIST "the time when the person attains the age of 18 years or sooner marries, or any time after either event"
        `what the entry points at`                        IS EMPTY
-- Worked out in ie-operation-and-construction.l4 (`the day on which the person attains full age`).

-- src:252 | “functions” includes powers and duties, and references to the performance of functions include, with respect to powers and duties, references to the exercise of the powers and the carrying out of the duties;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "functions" (src:252)
`Part 2 entry: functions` MEANS
    `An entry in the Schedule` WITH
        `the word defined`                                IS "functions"
        `the part of the Schedule`                        IS 2
        `how the entry gives the meaning`                 IS `the entry says it includes`
        `the case or context in which the entry applies`  IS NOTHING
        `the things the entry names`                      IS LIST "powers and duties", "powers", "duties", "the exercise of the powers and the carrying out of the duties", "the exercise of the powers", "the carrying out of the duties"
        `what the entry points at`                        IS EMPTY

-- F48: the members are the items as the line prints them AND the things each lists. The first three are what "functions" includes; the last three are what, with respect to
-- powers and duties, a reference to the performance of functions includes.

-- src:253 | “Member State” means, where the context so admits, a Member State of the European Communities or of the European Union;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "Member State" (src:253)
`Part 2 entry: Member State` MEANS
    `An entry in the Schedule` WITH
        `the word defined`                                IS "Member State"
        `the part of the Schedule`                        IS 2
        `how the entry gives the meaning`                 IS `the entry says it means`
        `the case or context in which the entry applies`  IS JUST "where the context so admits"
        `the things the entry names`                      IS LIST "a Member State of the European Communities or of the European Union"
        `what the entry points at`                        IS EMPTY

-- src:254 | “Minister of State” means a person appointed under section 1 of the Ministers and Secretaries (Amendment) (No. 2) Act 1977 to be a Minister of State;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "Minister of State" (src:254)
`Part 2 entry: Minister of State` MEANS
    `An entry in the Schedule` WITH
        `the word defined`                                IS "Minister of State"
        `the part of the Schedule`                        IS 2
        `how the entry gives the meaning`                 IS `the entry says it means`
        `the case or context in which the entry applies`  IS NOTHING
        `the things the entry names`                      IS LIST "a person appointed under section 1 of the Ministers and Secretaries (Amendment) (No. 2) Act 1977 to be a Minister of State"
        `what the entry points at`                        IS LIST "section 1 of the Ministers and Secretaries (Amendment) (No. 2) Act 1977"

-- src:255 | “public holiday” means a public holiday determined in accordance with the Organisation of Working Time Act 1997 ;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "public holiday" (src:255)
`Part 2 entry: public holiday` MEANS
    `An entry in the Schedule` WITH
        `the word defined`                                IS "public holiday"
        `the part of the Schedule`                        IS 2
        `how the entry gives the meaning`                 IS `the entry says it means`
        `the case or context in which the entry applies`  IS NOTHING
        `the things the entry names`                      IS LIST "a public holiday determined in accordance with the Organisation of Working Time Act 1997"
        `what the entry points at`                        IS LIST "the Organisation of Working Time Act 1997"
-- Worked out in ie-interpretation-time.l4 as an INPUT (`is a working day`): the 1997 Act is not in the text.

-- src:256 | “Social Welfare Acts” means the Social Welfare (Consolidation) Act 1993 and every other enactment which is to be read together with that Act;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "Social Welfare Acts" (src:256)
`Part 2 entry: Social Welfare Acts` MEANS
    `An entry in the Schedule` WITH
        `the word defined`                                IS "Social Welfare Acts"
        `the part of the Schedule`                        IS 2
        `how the entry gives the meaning`                 IS `the entry says it means`
        `the case or context in which the entry applies`  IS NOTHING
        `the things the entry names`                      IS LIST "the Social Welfare (Consolidation) Act 1993", "every other enactment which is to be read together with that Act"
        `what the entry points at`                        IS LIST "the Social Welfare (Consolidation) Act 1993"

-- src:257 | “working day” means a day which is not a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "working day" (src:257)
`Part 2 entry: working day` MEANS
    `An entry in the Schedule` WITH
        `the word defined`                                IS "working day"
        `the part of the Schedule`                        IS 2
        `how the entry gives the meaning`                 IS `the entry says it means`
        `the case or context in which the entry applies`  IS NOTHING
        `the things the entry names`                      IS LIST "a day which is not a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday"
        `what the entry points at`                        IS EMPTY
-- Worked out in ie-interpretation-time.l4 (`is a working day`).

-- src:186 | (2) In an enactment which comes into operation after the commencement of this Act, a word or expression to which a particular meaning, construction or effect is assigned in Part 2 of the Schedule has the meaning, construction or effect so assigned to it.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 21(2) (src:186)
GIVEN w IS A `A word defined in Part 2 of the Schedule`
GIVETH AN `An entry in the Schedule`
`the Part 2 entry for` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `Companies Acts`                        THEN `Part 2 entry: Companies Acts`
    WHEN `full age`                              THEN `Part 2 entry: full age`
    WHEN `functions`                             THEN `Part 2 entry: functions`
    WHEN `Member State`                          THEN `Part 2 entry: Member State`
    WHEN `Minister of State`                     THEN `Part 2 entry: Minister of State`
    WHEN `public holiday`                        THEN `Part 2 entry: public holiday`
    WHEN `Social Welfare Acts`                   THEN `Part 2 entry: Social Welfare Acts`
    WHEN `working day`                           THEN `Part 2 entry: working day`

§ `Entries that say what a word includes or does not include`

-- F47: an entry that says "includes" is read as an open list, so a thing it does not name refuses; an entry that says "does not include" excludes only what it names, so another thing refuses.
-- An entry that says it includes in a stated case or context gives nothing when the case or context does not exist (FALSE: the entry does not give the inclusion).

-- src:217 | “affidavit”, in the case of a person for the time being allowed by law to declare instead of swearing, includes declaration;
-- src:226 | “Great Britain” does not include the Channel Islands or the Isle of Man;
-- src:228 | “land” includes tenements, hereditaments, houses and buildings, land covered by water and any estate, right or interest in or over land;
-- src:233 | “oath”, in the case of a person for the time being allowed by law to affirm or declare instead of swearing, includes affirmation or declaration;
-- src:244 | “swear”, in the case of a person for the time being allowed by law to affirm or declare instead of swearing, includes affirm and declare;
-- src:247 | “writing” includes printing, typewriting, lithography, photography, and other modes of representing or reproducing words in visible form and any information kept in a non-legible form, whether stored electronically or otherwise, which is capable by any means of being reproduced in a legible form;
-- src:252 | “functions” includes powers and duties, and references to the performance of functions include, with respect to powers and duties, references to the exercise of the powers and the carrying out of the duties;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "affidavit", "Great Britain", "land", "oath", "swear", "writing"; Pt 2 "functions" (src:217, src:226, src:228, src:233, src:244, src:247, src:252)
GIVEN e IS AN `An entry in the Schedule`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the entry states a case or context` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e's `the case or context in which the entry applies`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST c   THEN TRUE

-- src:217 | “affidavit”, in the case of a person for the time being allowed by law to declare instead of swearing, includes declaration;
-- src:226 | “Great Britain” does not include the Channel Islands or the Isle of Man;
-- src:228 | “land” includes tenements, hereditaments, houses and buildings, land covered by water and any estate, right or interest in or over land;
-- src:233 | “oath”, in the case of a person for the time being allowed by law to affirm or declare instead of swearing, includes affirmation or declaration;
-- src:244 | “swear”, in the case of a person for the time being allowed by law to affirm or declare instead of swearing, includes affirm and declare;
-- src:247 | “writing” includes printing, typewriting, lithography, photography, and other modes of representing or reproducing words in visible form and any information kept in a non-legible form, whether stored electronically or otherwise, which is capable by any means of being reproduced in a legible form;
-- src:252 | “functions” includes powers and duties, and references to the performance of functions include, with respect to powers and duties, references to the exercise of the powers and the carrying out of the duties;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "affidavit", "Great Britain", "land", "oath", "swear", "writing"; Pt 2 "functions" (src:217, src:226, src:228, src:233, src:244, src:247, src:252)
GIVEN e IS AN `An entry in the Schedule`
      thing IS A STRING
      `the case or context stated in the entry exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the entry names the thing` e thing `the case or context stated in the entry exists` MEANS
    CONSIDER e's `how the entry gives the meaning`
    WHEN `the entry says it includes` THEN
        BRANCH IF `the entry states a case or context` e AND NOT `the case or context stated in the entry exists` THEN FALSE
               IF elem thing (e's `the things the entry names`) THEN TRUE
               OTHERWISE `an entry that says includes does not close the list, so a thing it does not name is not answered`
    WHEN `the entry says it does not include` THEN
        BRANCH IF elem thing (e's `the things the entry names`) THEN FALSE
               OTHERWISE `an entry that says does not include excludes only what it names, so another thing is not answered`
    WHEN `the entry says it means` THEN
        `an entry that says what a word means is not a list of inclusions`

§ `President, Minister of the Government and Constitution`

-- src:236 | “President” means the President of Ireland or any Commission, or other body or authority, for the time being lawfully exercising the powers and performing the duties of the President;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "President" (src:236)
GIVEN `it is the President of Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a Commission, or other body or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the time being lawfully exercising the powers of the President` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the time being lawfully performing the duties of the President` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is the President within the meaning of the Schedule` `it is the President of Ireland` `it is a Commission, or other body or authority` `it is for the time being lawfully exercising the powers of the President` `it is for the time being lawfully performing the duties of the President` MEANS
        `it is the President of Ireland`
     OR (    `it is a Commission, or other body or authority`
         AND `it is for the time being lawfully exercising the powers of the President`
         AND `it is for the time being lawfully performing the duties of the President`)

-- src:231 | “Minister of the Government” means a member of the Government having charge of a Department of State;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "Minister of the Government" (src:231)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has charge of a Department of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a Minister of the Government` `the person is a member of the Government` `the person has charge of a Department of State` MEANS
        `the person is a member of the Government`
    AND `the person has charge of a Department of State`

-- src:221 | “Constitution” means the Constitution of Ireland enacted by the people on 1 July 1937, as amended;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "Constitution" (src:221)
GIVEN `it is the Constitution of Ireland enacted by the people` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the people enacted it` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is the Constitution within the meaning of the Schedule` `it is the Constitution of Ireland enacted by the people` `the day on which the people enacted it` MEANS
        `it is the Constitution of Ireland enacted by the people`
    AND `the day on which the people enacted it` EQUALS YMD 1937 7 1

§ `Pre-union Irish statute`

-- src:237 | “pre-union Irish statute” means an Act passed by a Parliament sitting in Ireland at any time before the coming into force on 1 January 1801 of the Act entitled “An Act for the Union of Great Britain and Ireland”;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 1 "pre-union Irish statute" (src:237)
GIVEN `it is an Act passed by a Parliament sitting in Ireland` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a pre-union Irish statute` `it is an Act passed by a Parliament sitting in Ireland` `the day it was passed` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `it is an Act passed by a Parliament sitting in Ireland` THEN FALSE
           IF `the day it was passed` LESS THAN YMD 1801 1 1 THEN TRUE
           IF `the day it was passed` GREATER THAN YMD 1801 1 1 THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE `the entry gives no day within 1 January 1801 at which the Act of Union came into force, so an Act passed on that day is not answered`

§ `Companies Acts, Social Welfare Acts and Member State`

-- src:250 | “Companies Acts” means the Companies Acts 1963 to 2001 and every other enactment which is to be read together with any of those Acts;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "Companies Acts" (src:250)
GIVEN `it is one of the Companies Acts 1963 to 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is another enactment which is to be read together with any of those Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is within the Companies Acts as the Schedule defines them` `it is one of the Companies Acts 1963 to 2001` `it is another enactment which is to be read together with any of those Acts` MEANS
        `it is one of the Companies Acts 1963 to 2001`
     OR `it is another enactment which is to be read together with any of those Acts`

-- src:256 | “Social Welfare Acts” means the Social Welfare (Consolidation) Act 1993 and every other enactment which is to be read together with that Act;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "Social Welfare Acts" (src:256)
GIVEN `it is the Social Welfare (Consolidation) Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is another enactment which is to be read together with that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is within the Social Welfare Acts as the Schedule defines them` `it is the Social Welfare (Consolidation) Act 1993` `it is another enactment which is to be read together with that Act` MEANS
        `it is the Social Welfare (Consolidation) Act 1993`
     OR `it is another enactment which is to be read together with that Act`

-- src:253 | “Member State” means, where the context so admits, a Member State of the European Communities or of the European Union;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "Member State" (src:253)
GIVEN `it is a Member State of the European Communities or of the European Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context so admits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a Member State within the meaning of the Schedule` `it is a Member State of the European Communities or of the European Union` `the context so admits` MEANS
        `the context so admits`
    AND `it is a Member State of the European Communities or of the European Union`

§ `Sections 21(1) and 21(2): when a word of the Schedule has its meaning in an enactment`

-- src:185 | Interpretation of words and expressions in Schedule. 21.—(1) In an enactment, a word or expression to which a particular meaning, construction or effect is assigned in Part 1 of the Schedule has the meaning, construction or effect so assigned to it.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 21(1), subject to s 4(1) (src:185)
GIVEN w IS A `A word defined in Part 1 of the Schedule`
      where IS A `Where a contrary intention appears`
GIVETH A MAYBE `An entry in the Schedule`
`section 21(1) gives the Part 1 word its meaning in the enactment` w where MEANS
    IF   `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` where
    THEN JUST (`the Part 1 entry for` w)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:186 | (2) In an enactment which comes into operation after the commencement of this Act, a word or expression to which a particular meaning, construction or effect is assigned in Part 2 of the Schedule has the meaning, construction or effect so assigned to it.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 21(2), subject to s 4(1) (src:186)
GIVEN w IS A `A word defined in Part 2 of the Schedule`
      facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
      where IS A `Where a contrary intention appears`
GIVETH A MAYBE `An entry in the Schedule`
`section 21(2) gives the Part 2 word its meaning in the enactment` w facts where MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `a provision of this Act applies to an enactment` where THEN NOTHING
           IF `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` facts THEN JUST (`the Part 2 entry for` w)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING
